title: The Red Renaissance

# Counterfactual arc researched 16 August 2026. The organisations and people
# below are factual; their merger into a mass party is the alternate-history
# consequence of the player's sustained progressive wave.
# Akcja's programme and worker-movement strategy https://akcjasocjalistyczna.pl/
# Akcja's nine regions and new Tricity, Wrocław and Lublin groups in May 2025 https://akcjasocjalistyczna.pl/5-lat-akcji-socjalistycznej/
# Paweł Preneta: Akcja author and former/current Razem national councillor https://akcjasocjalistyczna.pl/author/pawe_preneta/ https://partiarazem.pl/o-nas/rada-krajowa
# Piotr and Agata Nosal-Ikonowicz's independent social-justice office https://fundacjakss.pl/
# Student housing occupations and Young IP groups https://ozzip.pl/publikacje/ksiazki-i-broszury/item/3079-kamionka-zostanie-rok-okupacji
# Inicjatywa Pracownicza's anarcho-syndicalist lineage https://ozzip.pl/inicjatywa-pracownicza/
# ZSP's anti-party independence https://zsp.net.pl/union-syndicalists-poland-zsp
# Federacja Anarchistyczna https://federacja-anarchistyczna.pl/
# Party freedom, Article 13 and Constitutional Tribunal jurisdiction https://trybunal.gov.pl/o-trybunale/akty-normatywne/konstytucja-rzeczypospolitej-polskiej/rozdzial-i https://trybunal.gov.pl/o-trybunale/trybunal-konstytucyjny-w-polsce/kompetencje-trybunalu-konstytucyjnego

@red_smoke
# prose-audit: Grade A — The rumour arrives through named organisers, a booked route and a coach list; the progressive wave and May Day history appear as political causes rather than exposed counters.
title: There are more red flags than ours
subtitle: A coach list and a Warsaw route turn socialist gossip into a date
face-image: img/poland/events/union-march.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_reactive
priority: 30
order: 8
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year >= 2025 and year <= 2027 and election_2027_terminal = 0 and red_renaissance_stage = 0 and public_climate_direction = "progressive wave" and public_climate_progressive_index >= 58 and public_climate_left_ownership_index >= 36 and progressive_credibility >= 58 and labor_credibility >= 52 and (government_delivery >= 8 or public_trust >= 52 or labor_day_union_years + labor_day_revival_years + labor_day_autonomous_years >= 3)
on-arrival: {!
const redMayDay = Math.min(
    14,
    (Number(Q.labor_day_union_years) || 0) * 2 +
    (Number(Q.labor_day_autonomous_years) || 0) * 3 +
    (Number(Q.labor_day_revival_years) || 0)
);
const redDelivery = Math.min(
    12,
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.government_delivery) || 0) * 0.30 +
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.public_trust) || 45) - 45) * 0.18
);
const successorOccupied = Q.tak_dla_rozwoju_party_formed &&
    Q.tak_rozwoj_party_name != "Akcja Socjalistyczna";
Q.red_renaissance_identity = Q.razem_party_formed || successorOccupied
    ? "Razem" : "Akcja Socjalistyczna";
Q.red_renaissance_leader = Q.red_renaissance_identity == "Razem"
    ? "Adrian Zandberg" : "Paweł Preneta";
Q.red_renaissance_stage = 1;
Q.red_renaissance_active = 1;
Q.red_renaissance_launch_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.red_renaissance_next_time = (Number(Q.time) || 0) + 1;
Q.red_renaissance_launch_index =
    Number(Q.public_climate_progressive_index) || 58;
Q.red_renaissance_mayday_bonus = redMayDay;
Q.red_renaissance_strength = Math.round(Math.max(
    10,
    Math.min(
        40,
        10 + redMayDay + redDelivery +
        Math.max(0, Q.red_renaissance_launch_index - 56) * 1.4
    )
));
Q.red_renaissance_outcome = "Rumours of a socialist convergence";
Q.news_headline = "A progressive wave produces rumours of a party beyond Lewica";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — Somebody has booked the coaches

The first report reaches us from Poznań. Organisers who defended the **Jowita**
dormitory are sharing a coach list with the people around Kraków's **Kamionka**.
Young Inicjatywa Pracownicza has added workplace contacts. Federacja
Anarchistyczna sections are discussing stewards. **Inicjatywa Pracownicza** and
**Związek Syndykalistów Polski** both insist that no party will command their
unions; both have asked what time the Warsaw route begins.

There is now a date, a meeting point and a draft call for public housing,
worker control, a shorter working week and trade-union rights. There is still
no membership roll. The distinction matters. A demonstration can be cancelled
without dissolving anything, and every organisation on the list has survived
larger parties trying to own it.

[? if red_renaissance_mayday_bonus >= 5: We recognise the names because our
May Days put them in the same trains, steward briefings and legal-observer
groups. Lewica rebuilt a piece of national movement infrastructure. Nobody
said its next invitation would carry our logo.?]
[? if red_renaissance_mayday_bonus < 5: The organisers have no national May
Day machine to inherit. Every coach, lawyer and sound system is being found
again, city by city. The list is shorter, but it belongs entirely to them.?]

[? if red_renaissance_identity = "Razem": Razem already left the common Left.
<span class="party party-razem"><b>Adrian Zandberg</b></span> has the registered
party, deputies and membership vote needed to turn the demonstration into
something permanent. If the convergence acquires a ballot line, it will be
**Razem**.?]
[? if red_renaissance_identity = "Akcja Socjalistyczna": Razem is still with
us, so the available vehicle is <span class="party party-name has-party-logo
party-akcja-socjalistyczna"><span class="party-name-logo"
aria-hidden="true"></span><b>Akcja Socjalistyczna</b></span>. **Paweł
Preneta** is circulating the organisational proposal; **Łukasz Kozak** is
working on the public declaration. An association built for socialist
education is being asked whether it wants members, candidates and accounts.?]

**Piotr Ikonowicz** endorses the demonstration for **Ruch Sprawiedliwości
Społecznej** and refuses a party post in the same conversation. He and **Agata
Nosal-Ikonowicz** keep KSS casework outside the project: a tenant who needs a
lawyer does not owe anybody a party card. For the moment, that is the shape of
the rumour—one route, several organisations and a name nobody has yet voted
to use.

- @red_smoke_help
- @red_smoke_claim
- @red_smoke_dismiss

@red_smoke_help
title: Quietly share stewards, lawyers and transport contacts
subtitle: Make the first mobilisation stronger while preserving formal distance.
on-arrival: red_renaissance_response = "Quiet logistical help"; red_renaissance_strength += 5; red_renaissance_city_network += 2; movement_autonomy += 3; organiser_energy += 2; resources -= 1 if resources >= 1; news_headline = "Lewica infrastructure helps a rival socialist mobilisation assemble"

Our organisers send the route plan, steward ratios and legal contacts without
a Lewica header. The demonstration becomes safer and larger. It also acquires
the most useful sentence in a founding argument: even people inside Lewica
thought the new mobilisation ought to happen.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_smoke_claim
title: Publish our delivery ledger before the rumour becomes their story
subtitle: Argue that power and implementation, not maximal distance, made the wave possible.
on-arrival: red_renaissance_response = "Claim the progressive record"; public_trust += 2; government_delivery += 1 if left_in_government = 1; progressive_credibility += 1; red_renaissance_strength -= 1; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "Lewica answers socialist rumours with a ledger of delivered reforms"

The press office is told to list only measures with a date, a vote and an
implementing office. Announcements do not count. The answer accepts the
movement's premise—that organisation wins things—and asks why the organisation
that won them should be replaced.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_smoke_dismiss
title: Treat it as another Warsaw reading group
subtitle: Keep the party above a rumour and let the organisers define what the silence means.
on-arrival: red_renaissance_response = "Public dismissal"; red_renaissance_strength += 3; red_renaissance_city_network += 1; young_support -= 1; barons_dissent -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica dismisses the rumoured socialist convergence"

The press office calls it a Warsaw reading group. By evening the sentence sits
above photographs of Jowita, Kamionka, a strike collection and a steward
briefing. The organisers had a route and a grievance; we have supplied an
opponent.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_withering
# prose-audit: Grade A — The collapse is shown through cancelled coaches, a lost hall and organisations returning to their own work, not through an exposed support score.
title: The red spring dries before summer
subtitle: A fast mood reversal makes the rumoured convergence wither before it becomes a party
