on-arrival: {!
Q.red_renaissance_stage = 3;
Q.red_renaissance_next_time = (Number(Q.time) || 0) + 1;
Q.red_renaissance_city_network += 6 + Math.round(
    (Number(Q.red_renaissance_mayday_bonus) || 0) * 0.35
);
Q.red_renaissance_strength += 4;
Q.red_renaissance_voter_theft += 2;
if (Q.red_renaissance_identity == "Razem") Q.razem_poll_momentum += 0.5;
else Q.tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += 0.5;
Q.poll_state_month_key = -1;
Q.news_headline = "The Red Renaissance opens organising rooms across Poland's major cities";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — Six sets of keys

Warsaw opens above a tenant advice office. Poznań shares a corridor with
organisers from Jowita and workplace committees; Kraków begins with the
Kamionka occupation's phone tree. Łódź finds a room through trade unionists.
The Wrocław and Tricity groups arrive with university contacts, port workers
and the least patience for Warsaw deciding what a region is for.

Every branch is required to hold three things each week: a public advice hour,
a political meeting and work on one live dispute. That rule matters more than
the opening photographs. A person may enter over an eviction, an unpaid wage
or a dormitory closure and return for a meeting whose minutes include a
candidate selection.

[? if red_renaissance_mayday_bonus >= 5: The May Day network means the rooms
open with trained stewards and inter-city transport. The first national
briefing uses the coach captains and legal observers our own marches trained.?]
[? if red_renaissance_mayday_bonus < 5: The organisers lack a national May Day
machine, so they substitute slow local work. The result is smaller, harder to
photograph and more difficult to uproot.?]

The competition is visible before a vote is taken. When we announce a housing
bill they read it with tenants that evening. When our minister visits a strike
they publish the clause the coalition removed. When we call a rally they book
the following night and ask what the rally changed.

- @red_cities_delivery
- @red_cities_platforms
- @red_cities_fight

@red_cities_delivery
title: Put local delivery teams beside every rival branch
subtitle: Compete case by case in housing, labour inspection and public services.
on-arrival: red_renaissance_response = "Local delivery competition"; local_network += 4; labor_credibility += 2; household_security += 1; red_renaissance_voter_theft -= 1; red_renaissance_city_network += 1; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "Lewica answers rival socialist rooms with local delivery teams"

Our councillors, lawyers and constituency offices receive one shared case
queue and a forty-eight-hour reply rule. The answer is unglamorous and exact:
the office that keeps a family housed or recovers an unpaid wage receives the
next call, whatever was said at the larger meeting.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_cities_platforms
title: Share anti-eviction and strike platforms without sharing a list
subtitle: Let the movement grow where action requires unity and preserve electoral competition.
on-arrival: red_renaissance_response = "Common movement platforms"; movement_autonomy += 5; union_trust += 3; organiser_energy += 3; red_renaissance_strength += 4; red_renaissance_city_network += 3; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica and the Red Renaissance share movement platforms but not a ballot"

The flags mix outside a landlord's office and separate before the press
conference. RSS lawyers take cases from both sets of organisers; the unions
send their own speaker and endorse neither list. The eviction is stopped. Both
party offices spend the evening checking whose volunteers kept the contacts.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_cities_fight
title: Challenge every branch for ownership of the progressive wave
subtitle: Build our own crowd and turn each campaign into a test of strength.
