Our regional secretaries are told to contest every public meeting with an
organiser and every campaign with a better offer. Attendance rises because
each side brings people to answer the other. So does duplication: two legal
teams, two coach lists and two speeches outside the same workplace.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_government_protest
# prose-audit: Grade A — The rival's first national march is no longer generic atmosphere: it selects the player's strongest live failure, names the responsible office, scales turnout from the organisation actually built, and makes the government answer a crowd assembled against it.
title: The first Red Renaissance march is against us
subtitle: The new party turns our weakest live government record into a national demonstration
face-image: img/poland/events/union-march.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
priority: 31
order: 8
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and red_renaissance_stage = 3 and left_in_government = 1 and time >= red_renaissance_next_time
on-arrival: {!
const redFollowthrough = String(
    Q.movement_followthrough_2025 || ""
).toLowerCase();
const redRightsBroken = [
    "breach", "failed", "defeat", "rejected", "veto"
].some(function(word) { return redFollowthrough.includes(word); });
const redPartnershipFailed = Number(Q.year) >= 2026 &&
    Q.partnership_strategy != "No parliamentary strategy" &&
    !Q.partnership_sejm_passed;
const redBurdenFailures = Math.max(
    0, Number(Q.government_burden_failures) || 0
);
const redReviewFailed = redBurdenFailures > 0 && (
    String(Q.government_burden_last_result || "").includes("fails") ||
    String(Q.government_burden_last_result || "").includes("misses")
);
const redGrievances = [
    {
        key: "rights",
        label: "the broken equality and reproductive-rights promise",
        minister: String(Q.equality_minister || Q.labor_minister || Q.prime_minister),
        score: redRightsBroken ? 48 : (redPartnershipFailed ? 36 : 0),
        record: redRightsBroken
            ? String(Q.movement_followthrough_2025)
            : String(Q.partnership_strategy)
    },
    {
        key: "government_record",
        label: "Lewica's failed six-month social record",
        minister: String(Q.prime_minister || "the Prime Minister"),
        score: redReviewFailed
            ? 24 + redBurdenFailures * 6 +
                (Q.government_burden_last_breached ? 12 : 0) +
                Math.max(
                    0,
                    (Number(Q.government_burden_required) || 2) -
                    (Number(Q.government_burden_last_completed) || 0)
                ) * 5
            : (Q.government_burden_breached ? 20 : 0),
        record: String(
            Q.government_burden_last_result || "No completed review"
        )
    },
    {
        key: "housing",
        label: "rents, evictions and the missing public homes",
        minister: String(Q.housing_minister || Q.prime_minister),
        score: Math.max(8, 55 - (Number(Q.household_security) || 45)) +
            (Q.government_goal_housing ? 0 : 8) +
            (Q.government_burden_tenant_seen ? 3 : 0),
        record: "Housing and tenant security remain the largest material gap"
    },
    {
        key: "health",
        label: "hospital queues and the public-service settlement",
        minister: String(Q.health_minister || Q.prime_minister),
        score: Math.max(6, 54 - (Number(Q.health_capacity) || 48)) +
            (Q.government_goal_health ? 0 : 7) +
            (Q.marketisation_concessions ? 6 : 0),
        record: "The public system still carries the queues and staffing gap"
    },
    {
        key: "labour",
        label: "labour inspection, bargaining rights and public pay",
        minister: String(Q.labor_minister || Q.prime_minister),
        score: 8 + Math.max(0, Number(Q.labor_dissent) || 0) * 0.35 +
            (Q.government_goal_labor ? 0 : 7) +
            (Q.government_burden_social_delay_seen ? 3 : 0),
        record: "Workplace enforcement remains behind the government's promises"
    }
].sort(function(a, b) { return b.score - a.score; });
const redGrievance = redGrievances[0];
const redTurnout = Math.round(Math.min(
    140000,
    Math.max(
        14000,
        8000 + (Number(Q.red_renaissance_strength) || 0) * 950 +
        (Number(Q.red_renaissance_city_network) || 0) * 1100 +
        redGrievance.score * 420 +
        (Number(Q.red_renaissance_mayday_bonus) || 0) * 450
    )
) / 1000) * 1000;
Q.red_renaissance_stage = 4;
Q.red_renaissance_next_time = (Number(Q.time) || 0) + 1;
Q.red_renaissance_protest_issue = redGrievance.key;
Q.red_renaissance_protest_demand = redGrievance.label;
Q.red_renaissance_protest_record = redGrievance.record;
Q.red_renaissance_protest_minister = redGrievance.minister;
Q.red_renaissance_protest_turnout = redTurnout;
Q.red_renaissance_protest_scale = redTurnout >= 75000
    ? "a march filling central Warsaw"
    : (redTurnout >= 40000
        ? "a national march several streets long"
        : "a five-city mobilisation converging on Warsaw");
Q.red_renaissance_strength += 4;
Q.red_renaissance_voter_theft += Math.max(2, redTurnout / 30000);
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
if (Q.red_renaissance_identity == "Razem") {
    Q.razem_poll_momentum += Math.min(1.4, redTurnout / 80000);
} else {
    Q.tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += Math.min(1.4, redTurnout / 80000);
}
Q.poll_state_month_key = -1;
Q.news_headline = "The Red Renaissance marches against the government over " +
    Q.red_renaissance_protest_demand;
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The first march is aimed at our ministries

At ten in the morning the coaches begin unloading beside Warszawa Centralna.
The stewards wear the new party's red bibs, not ours. Poznań carries a Jowita
banner, Kraków a Kamionka banner, and the workplace columns arrive behind the
flags of unions that have refused every offer of party discipline. The route
ends outside the Chancellery. This is **[+ red_renaissance_protest_scale +]**,
roughly **[+ red_renaissance_protest_turnout +] people**, organised by a party
that did not exist a few months ago.

[? if red_renaissance_protest_issue = "government_record": The organisers
print our own half-year verdict across the front leaflet: **[+
red_renaissance_protest_record +]**. The cabinet may dispute who blocked which
bill; it cannot dispute the review it published. **[+ prime_minister +]** is
named because coalition government has finally produced a record with an
owner.?]
[? if red_renaissance_protest_issue = "rights": The front banner quotes the
promise and the result underneath it: **[+ red_renaissance_protest_record +]**.
Feminist and equality organisers who once stood beside Lewica now lead the
column asking why office turned a deadline into another explanation.?]
[? if red_renaissance_protest_issue = "housing": The march stops at a block
where tenants have received another rent increase and the municipal waiting
list has not moved. Housing Minister **[+ red_renaissance_protest_minister +]**
is asked for the homes, tenant guarantees and eviction rules that survived the
coalition table—not the number of meetings held about them.?]
[? if red_renaissance_protest_issue = "health": Hospital-union placards put
vacancies and waiting lists beside the cabinet's announcements. Health
Minister **[+ red_renaissance_protest_minister +]** is accused of finding room
for compromise before finding staff for the public wards.?]
[? if red_renaissance_protest_issue = "labour": Inspectors, public-service
workers and workplace organisers carry the dates on which enforcement and pay
were meant to improve. Labour Minister **[+ red_renaissance_protest_minister
+]** now faces the people for whom an undated reform is simply a refusal in
better stationery.?]

[? if red_renaissance_mayday_bonus >= 5: The painful part is logistical. The
coach captains, legal observers and sound crews learned the work on May Days
we helped rebuild. Our success supplied the movement with a national address
book; its first independent use is a demonstration against us.?]
[? if red_renaissance_mayday_bonus < 5: The party had to assemble the route
city by city. That makes the turnout less polished and more dangerous: nobody
at headquarters can identify a single organisation whose withdrawal would
empty the street.?]

**Piotr Ikonowicz** speaks from the RSS column and takes no place on the party
platform. KSS lawyers work the route as outside legal observers. When **[+
red_renaissance_leader +]** reaches the microphone, the demand is not that the
government become less right-wing. It is that a government containing Lewica
answer for **[+ red_renaissance_protest_demand +]**.

- @red_protest_deadline
- @red_protest_open
- @red_protest_cordon

