on-arrival: red_renaissance_stage = 6; red_renaissance_next_time = time + 1; razem_dissent += 10; razem_cooperation -= 6; red_renaissance_strength += 3; tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += 0.5; poll_state_month_key = -1; news_headline = "Razem members debate whether Akcja now carries their original purpose"

= [+ date_label +] — The National Council agenda is no longer procedural

Razem stayed inside Lewica. The decision prevented a parliamentary split and
left its members in the rooms where coalition policy is written. It also means
that Akcja can now stand outside those rooms, quote each concession and ask
which organisation is doing the work Razem was founded to do.

The first motion comes from local branches whose members attend Akcja schools
and demonstrations: permit public organising in both organisations while
protecting membership data. The second comes from members who want no dual
cards at all: bind Lewica to a socialist minimum on ownership, housing and
labour, or prepare an orderly exit. Preneta offers no immediate merger. He
offers joint campaigns and a congress after the next recruitment report.

Zandberg must put a rule to the National Council. A membership question has
become a judgment on whether remaining inside Lewica changes the government or
only supplies socialist votes for its compromises.

- @red_razem_dual
- @red_razem_floor
- @red_razem_discipline

@red_razem_dual
title: Permit dual organising while banning transfers of member data
subtitle: Lower the immediate revolt and let Akcja recruit in the same rooms.
on-arrival: razem_dissent -= 5; razem_cooperation += 2; movement_autonomy += 3; red_renaissance_strength += 5; red_renaissance_voter_theft += 2; tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += 0.5; news_headline = "Razem permits transparent dual organising with Akcja Socjalistyczna"

Members may work on public campaigns in both organisations, but neither may
copy rolls, collect the other's dues or claim authority over its vote. The
rule prevents a midnight transfer. It also makes every shared campaign a place
where members can compare which card they intend to keep.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_razem_floor
title: Put a binding socialist floor to the whole Left
subtitle: Make public ownership, housing and labour milestones conditions of continued unity.
on-arrival: razem_dissent -= 9; razem_cooperation += 5; hard_left_line += 1; hard_left_turn_open = 1; barons_dissent += 6; government_coalition_dissent += 4 if left_in_government = 1; tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum -= 0.3; left_poll_momentum += 0.25; poll_state_month_key = -1; news_headline = "A binding socialist floor keeps Razem inside Lewica"

The adopted floor names sectors for public ownership, a housing target and a
date for labour enforcement. Razem can now point to a document binding the
whole Left; our coalition partners can point to its price. Akcja loses the
claim that only an outside party can write such terms and keeps the evidence
that outside pressure forced the vote.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_razem_discipline
title: Require one party card and enforce caucus discipline
subtitle: Clarify membership by turning wavering into departure pressure.
on-arrival: razem_dissent += 12; razem_cooperation -= 8; party_unity += 2; barons_dissent -= 2; red_renaissance_strength += 6; red_renaissance_voter_theft += 3; tak_rozwoj_poll_momentum += 0.8; poll_state_month_key = -1; news_headline = "Lewica discipline pushes wavering Razem organisers toward Akcja"

The rule is easy to administer: one membership declaration and thirty days to
comply. It turns sympathy into a departure date. Nobody takes a parliamentary
mandate that night; the losses are branch officers, stewards, meeting rooms and
the story that Lewica answered a socialist challenge with an expulsion form.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_ban_debate
