= [+ date_label +] — A parliamentary quarrel becomes a legal file

PiS deputies begin collecting signatures for a Constitutional Tribunal
application. Konfederacja sends selected speeches to the prosecutor and calls
the party an openly revolutionary organisation. KO rejects a ban in its public
statement, then asks its lawyers for an opinion on the same statute, steward
manuals and demonstration footage. Three parties that disagree on the remedy
have agreed that the Red Renaissance is large enough to investigate.

The constitutional text is narrower than the television argument. Poland
protects democratic parties, unions and associations. Article 13 reaches
totalitarian methods, racial or national hatred, political violence and secret
structures or membership; the Constitutional Tribunal, not a party whip,
judges a party's aims and activity. The Red Renaissance publishes elected
bodies, open membership and a non-violence rule. Its anarchist and syndicalist
allies cite that transparency while refusing its discipline.

The file includes the march against our government. [? if
red_renaissance_response = "Restrict and denounce the march": It also includes
the route restriction we authorised, now cited as the first official warning
that the party threatened public order.?][? if red_renaissance_response !=
"Restrict and denounce the march": Its open route, published stewards and KSS
observers make the allegation harder to sustain.?]

Ikonowicz offers to testify about lawful anti-eviction resistance. Preneta or
Zandberg asks us to appear beside him. The request contains both a trap and a
principle: defend a rival and enlarge its platform, or let PiS and Konfederacja
define the civil liberty on which our own organisations depend.

- @red_ban_defend
- @red_ban_scrutinise
- @red_ban_bargain

@red_ban_defend
title: Defend democratic association without endorsing their programme
subtitle: Draw the constitutional line publicly and let the rival claim the shared platform.
on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 6; public_trust += 3; progressive_credibility += 3; red_renaissance_ban_pressure -= 8; red_renaissance_strength += 3; ko_relation += 1; pis_relation -= 3; konf_relation -= 4; news_headline = "Lewica defends the Red Renaissance's constitutional right to organise"

We read Articles 11, 12 and 13 together, publish the party statute beside them
and refuse guilt by adjective. The rival receives the joint photograph. We
keep the distinction between defeating a programme and asking the state to
erase the organisation that carries it.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_ban_scrutinise
title: Support a public evidence hearing on violence and transparent membership
subtitle: Apply one democratic standard to the movement, police and counter-demonstrators.
on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 3; police_trust += 1; public_trust += 1; red_renaissance_ban_pressure -= 12; red_renaissance_strength -= 2; movement_autonomy -= 1; news_headline = "A public evidence hearing replaces demands for an immediate socialist ban"

The hearing publishes police orders, steward logs, financial rules,
counter-demonstrator violence and the party statute. Every allegation receives
a document and an answer. The movement loses some useful ambiguity; its
enemies lose the secret file in which ambiguity could be made to prove
anything.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk

@red_ban_bargain
title: Trade a common civil-liberties front for electoral non-aggression
subtitle: Reduce legal pressure and make the new party negotiate where it contests.
on-arrival: red_renaissance_ban_pressure -= 6; public_trust += 1; party_unity -= 1; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; razem_party_relation += 6 if red_renaissance_identity = "Razem"; tak_rozwoj_parent_relation += 6 if red_renaissance_identity = "Akcja Socjalistyczna"; news_headline = "Civil-liberties cooperation opens electoral talks on the left"

We will oppose a ban. In return, the new party will meet over constituencies,
debate rules and a minimum non-aggression code. Nobody promises a common list.
The Red Renaissance remains a rival; it must now decide whether refusing every
agreement includes gifting seats to the parties that tried to remove it.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the events desk
